.TH ZEX-UPDATE 1 "2026-06-27" "zex 5.0.0" "Zainium OS"
.SH NAME
zex-update \- fetch latest index and upgrade all packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B elevate zex update
.RI [ \-\-yes ]
.RI [ \-\-uland\-only ]
.RI [ \-\-syshub\-only ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zex update
performs a full system update in two passes:
.TP
1.
Refresh the package index from all configured mirrors
.RI ( /overlayer/syshub/engine/services/zex_services.toml ).
.TP
2.
Diff the fresh index against installed packages and apply all available
upgrades, skipping any packages that are pinned.
.PP
Userland packages
.RI ( /overlayer/zexlib/union/ )
and the immutable syshub base
.RI ( /overlayer/syshub/ )
are updated in separate phases. The syshub phase uses an atomic
swap: the new base is assembled in
.I /overlayer/syshub.new/
and then renamed to the live path, giving a crash-safe upgrade.
.PP
Archive extraction uses the same path-sanitization primitives as
.BR zex-install (1)
(traversal-safe symlink and hardlink targets), and registry updates go
through the same safe, receipt-aware registry writer rather than
patching TOML text directly. The pre-flight connectivity check tries
the Tier 1 (Zainium) archive first and falls back to a well-known
public mirror, so a slow or down Zainium endpoint alone does not cause
a spurious "no internet" abort.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-y, \-\-yes
Apply upgrades without prompting for confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-uland\-only
Only upgrade userland packages; skip syshub.
.TP
.B \-\-syshub\-only
Only upgrade the immutable base; skip userland.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Update completed (even if nothing needed upgrading).
.TP
.B 1
Network error, verification failure, or insufficient privileges.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
    elevate zex update
    elevate zex update --yes
    elevate zex update --uland-only
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zex (1),
.BR zex-rollback (1),
.BR zex-doctor (1)
